---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LeadForm from '../components/LeadForm.astro';
import { SCORECARDS_PER_WEEK } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Free Website Discoverability Scorecard"
  description="See how discoverable your site is to search engines and AI assistants, with the few fixes that matter most, ranked."
  scorecardCta={false}
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">Free scorecard</p>
        <h1>How discoverable is your website?</h1>
        <p class="lead-text">
          Our scorecard checks how well search engines and AI assistants can
          find, read, and understand your site, then ranks the few fixes that
          matter most. It's free, and we walk you through the results personally.
        </p>
        <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="#request">Request your scorecard →</a></p>

        <h2>What it checks</h2>
        <p>Results are grouped under the three things every website needs to be:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Discoverable:</strong> findability, AI readiness, and how
            your pages look when shared.
          </li>
          <li><strong>Actionable:</strong> whether visitors have a clear next step.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Relatable:</strong> whether your content has the depth to
            show people, and AI, what you actually do.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="note">
          This version focuses on discoverability from the outside. It doesn't
          need access to your accounts. Analytics and competitive context are
          coming in future versions.
        </p>

        <h2>What you get</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>A score, with what's working and what isn't</li>
          <li>Your top fixes, ranked by impact and effort</li>
          <li>A walkthrough call where we explain what we found</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How it works</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Send us your URL.</li>
          <li>We run the scorecard and review the results by hand.</li>
          <li>We walk through it together on a short call.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>We tried it on ourselves first</h2>
        <p>
          Our own site scored a 77.
          <a href="/fixing-it-in-public">See our score and what we're fixing →</a>
        </p>

        <h2 id="request">Request your scorecard</h2>
        <p>We run {SCORECARDS_PER_WEEK} scorecards a week, first come, first served.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: var(--bca-space-6);">
    <div class="wrap">
      <LeadForm type="scorecard" submitLabel="Request my scorecard →" />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
